---
description: Commit za*.md changes and follow deploy.md.
alwaysApply: true
---

Read the root `deploy.md` before committing, syncing, or deploying.

For every commit, include all repository files whose basename matches
`za*.md`, including new files, modifications, and tracked deletions at
any depth. Re-read their current contents and stage them immediately
before committing:

```bash
git add -A -- ':(glob)**/za*.md'
```

Unchanged files are already in the commit snapshot; do not edit them
just to produce a diff. Preserve the user's text and newer edits.
Stage other task files explicitly and review the full staged diff.
Do not sweep unrelated changes into the commit. If required files have
sensitive content, surface the conflict rather than silently exposing it.

Use the Git production hook for the website and rsync for `/my/md/`.
Do not publish the private `/my/` parent, caches, or credentials.
Commit and deploy only within the user's authorized task scope.
